paper-poker-rules =
    {"["}head=2]Texas Hold'em[/head]
    Remove the joker. Each player gets two private cards.
    The first two players clockwise from the dealer post the small and big blinds. With two players, the dealer posts the small blind.

    Bet after the deal. The dealer then reveals three community cards (the flop), followed by one card (the turn), then one more (the river). Bet after each reveal.
    On your turn, you can fold, call the current bet, raise it, or check if you owe nothing.
    If everyone else folds, you win the pot. Otherwise, make the best five-card hand from your private cards and the community cards.

    From weakest to strongest: high card, pair, two pair, three of a kind, straight, flush, full house, four of a kind, straight flush.
    An ace can start A–2–3–4–5 or finish 10–J–Q–K–A. Equal winning hands split the pot.

    Pass the dealer position clockwise after each hand.
